  <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.1] mb-6">Affiliate Disclosure</h1>

  <p class="text-lg text-2 mb-10">
    ACESLIVEPH is a media and information platform funded primarily through affiliate relationships with online poker rooms,
    casinos, and gambling-adjacent services. This page explains those relationships in detail so you can make informed decisions.
  </p>

  <h2>What "affiliate link" means</h2>
  <p>
    Some links on ACESLIVEPH — particularly on our review pages, comparison pages, and within editorial articles — are affiliate links.
    When you click an affiliate link and subsequently sign up and deposit at the linked operator, ACESLIVEPH receives a commission
    payment from that operator. <strong>This costs you nothing extra.</strong> The operator pays us for the referral; you pay
    the same prices and play the same games as you would by going directly to the operator.
  </p>

  <h2>Operators we have or are pursuing affiliate relationships with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>ClubGG Poker</li>
    <li>Natural8 (GGPoker Asia)</li>
    <li>ACR Poker (Americas Cardroom / WPN)</li>
    <li>WPT Global</li>
    <li>CoinPoker</li>
    <li>PokerStars</li>
    <li>Booking.com (hotels — when integrated)</li>
    <li>Agoda (hotels — when integrated)</li>
    <li>Selected training products (GTO Wizard, Run It Once, Upswing Poker, etc.)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The list above reflects active and intended relationships as of the last-updated date. Some are formally signed; others are in
    application stage. We will update this page as relationships are added or removed.
  </p>

  <h2>How affiliate relationships affect our coverage — they don't</h2>
  <p>
    ACESLIVEPH editorial reviews and rankings are produced independently of our affiliate relationships. Sites are ranked in the
    order we'd recommend them to a friend, not in the order that pays us most. We do not accept money to write a positive review of
    something we wouldn't have recommended unpaid.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is enforced through the following operating rules:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Editorial decisions about what to cover and how to rank operators are made before any affiliate negotiation.</li>
    <li>An operator's affiliate payout structure (CPA rate, revenue share, flat fees) does not influence ranking position.</li>
    <li>If an operator threatens to pull an affiliate deal because of editorial coverage, we publish the piece, end the affiliate relationship, and write a separate piece about the threat with documentation.</li>
    <li>Our ranking methodology is published in each review for transparency.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Sponsored content and how it differs</h2>
  <p>
    Separately from affiliate links, we sometimes publish sponsored content where an operator pays for placement of editorial-style content
    (e.g., a "Player Spotlight" featuring one of their sponsored players, or a featured listing on a review hub page).
  </p>
  <p>
    All sponsored content is clearly labeled <strong class="orange">"Sponsored"</strong> at the top of the post, in the URL meta-description,
    and (where applicable) verbally on YouTube videos. We retain editorial control over how sponsored content is framed; sponsors review only the
    factual accuracy of statements about themselves.
  </p>

  <h2>FTC and platform disclosure compliance</h2>
  <p>
    ACESLIVEPH targets a global audience including readers in the United States, the European Union, and the United Kingdom. We aim to
    comply with the disclosure standards of:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>US Federal Trade Commission "Endorsement Guides"</li>
    <li>UK Advertising Standards Authority CAP Code</li>
    <li>EU consumer protection directives on commercial communications</li>
    <li>Philippine SEC and DTI guidelines on advertising</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    In practice, this means: every page with affiliate links includes a clearly labeled disclosure box (like the one at the top of every review).
    Sponsored social media posts on Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, and X are tagged <code>#ad</code> or <code>#sponsored</code> per platform requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions or corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If you spot a missing disclosure, an outdated affiliate relationship, or have any concerns about how a piece of content was monetized,
    contact us at <a href="mailto:editorial@acesliveph.com">editorial@acesliveph.com</a>. We take affiliate transparency seriously and respond
    to every disclosure-related inquiry.
  </p>

